WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.176
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.476 --> 00:00:08.920
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:15.692
Unit thirteen: The Khmer Empire. In this unit, you will talk about the history of the Khmer Empire.

4
00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:17.592
Empire.

5
00:00:18.292 --> 00:00:21.766
Empire means a group of countries ruled by one king or government.

6
00:00:22.066 --> 00:00:24.123
The Khmer Empire was very powerful.

7
00:00:24.823 --> 00:00:27.011
Your turn. Say: Empire.

8
00:00:29.711 --> 00:00:30.608
Empire.

9
00:00:31.617 --> 00:00:32.339
King.

10
00:00:33.039 --> 00:00:35.097
King means a man who rules a country.

11
00:00:35.397 --> 00:00:38.453
King Jayavarman the Seventh built many temples.

12
00:00:39.153 --> 00:00:41.143
Your turn. Say: King.

13
00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:44.589
King.

14
00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:46.259
Temple.

15
00:00:46.959 --> 00:00:48.970
Temple means a building for religion.

16
00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:51.456
Bayon is a temple with many faces.

17
00:00:52.156 --> 00:00:54.564
Your turn. Say: Temple.

18
00:00:57.264 --> 00:00:57.998
Temple.

19
00:00:58.983 --> 00:00:59.775
Angkor.

20
00:01:00.475 --> 00:01:03.787
Angkor means the great old capital of the Khmer Empire.

21
00:01:04.087 --> 00:01:06.005
Millions of people visit Angkor.

22
00:01:06.705 --> 00:01:08.614
Your turn. Say: Angkor.

23
00:01:11.314 --> 00:01:12.060
Angkor.

24
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:13.784
Capital.

25
00:01:14.484 --> 00:01:17.180
Capital means the most important city of a country.

26
00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:19.561
Angkor was the capital of the empire.

27
00:01:20.261 --> 00:01:22.344
Your turn. Say: Capital.

28
00:01:25.044 --> 00:01:25.895
Capital.

29
00:01:26.883 --> 00:01:27.733
Ancient.

30
00:01:28.433 --> 00:01:31.153
Ancient means very, very old.

31
00:01:31.453 --> 00:01:33.313
Angkor Wat is an ancient temple.

32
00:01:34.013 --> 00:01:36.538
Your turn. Say: Ancient.

33
00:01:39.238 --> 00:01:40.204
Ancient.

34
00:01:41.217 --> 00:01:42.009
History.

35
00:01:42.709 --> 00:01:44.801
History means the study of the past.

36
00:01:45.101 --> 00:01:47.101
I love learning about Khmer history.

37
00:01:47.801 --> 00:01:50.546
Your turn. Say: History.

38
00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.061
History.

39
00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:55.958
Builders.

40
00:01:56.658 --> 00:01:59.006
Builders means people who make buildings.

41
00:01:59.306 --> 00:02:01.677
The builders used huge stones.

42
00:02:02.377 --> 00:02:05.134
Your turn. Say: Builders.

43
00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:08.765
Builders.

44
00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.866
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:12.166 --> 00:02:14.467
Sreypich, when was Angkor Wat built?

46
00:02:15.783 --> 00:02:17.853
It was built in the twelfth century.

47
00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:20.511
Who was it built by?

48
00:02:21.817 --> 00:02:25.894
It was built by King Suryavarman the Second and thousands of builders.

49
00:02:27.183 --> 00:02:28.173
And the Bayon?

50
00:02:29.483 --> 00:02:32.319
The Bayon was built by King Jayavarman the Seventh.

51
00:02:33.617 --> 00:02:36.951
Grammar focus: Past simple passive (was built).

52
00:02:37.251 --> 00:02:39.692
Angkor Wat was built in the twelfth century.

53
00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:42.920
Use the passive when the thing is more important than who did it.

54
00:02:43.917 --> 00:02:46.627
Now read and listen. The Great Khmer Empire.

55
00:02:46.927 --> 00:02:50.006
The Khmer Empire was one of the greatest empires in Asia.

56
00:02:51.317 --> 00:02:54.222
Its capital, Angkor, was a huge ancient city.

57
00:02:55.517 --> 00:02:59.014
Angkor Wat was built in the twelfth century by thousands of builders.

58
00:03:00.317 --> 00:03:03.210
The heavy stones were carried from a mountain far away.

59
00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:07.666
Today, Angkor is a symbol of Khmer history and pride.

60
00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.498
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:11.798 --> 00:03:14.122
Angkor Wat blank built in the 12th century.

62
00:03:14.422 --> 00:03:17.565
A, was. B, were. C, is.

63
00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.283
The answer is A: was.

64
00:03:24.783 --> 00:03:27.410
The most important city of a country is the blank.

65
00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:31.410
A, capital. B, temple. C, empire.

66
00:03:35.417 --> 00:03:37.497
The answer is A: capital.

67
00:03:38.983 --> 00:03:40.820
Very, very old means blank.

68
00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:45.134
A, ancient. B, historic. C, modern.

69
00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:51.347
The answer is A: ancient.

70
00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:56.431
Now it's your turn to speak. What do you know about the Khmer Empire?

71
00:04:01.731 --> 00:04:08.795
The Khmer Empire was very powerful. Angkor Wat was built in the twelfth century, and it is the biggest temple in the world.

72
00:04:09.095 --> 00:04:11.269
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:12.283 --> 00:04:17.246
Great work today! You learned eight new words and past simple passive (was built).

74
00:04:17.546 --> 00:04:22.160
Today's value is cultural pride. Be proud of Khmer festivals and traditions.

75
00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:25.032
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:25.332 --> 00:04:28.471
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

